class: negative
summary: [1800] writes a parameter's mode before its name, so `r: inout rec`, as Swift writes it, is refused once at the mode naming `inout r: rec`, with the move offered, and the named type after it is not refused again
program: program.ldn
codes: L0101
fixed: program.fixed
constructs: 0900, 1800
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, synthetic-32, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64
expect: expected.txt
args: ../tests/fixtures/negative/parameter-mode-after-the-colon-goes-first/program.ldn
status: 1
